    "body": "pulse task #2839 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:3193356d805e2e20eaa8ca89424157a2 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2839: Toggle Arrangement automation mode with A over faded clips\n\nOperation: 3193356d805e2e20eaa8ca89424157a2\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser request, 18 October 2026, with Ableton Live reference screenshot supplied in merger chat: A toggles Arrangement automation mode. Normal mode shows clips with normal clip editing. Automation mode fades the clips into the background and displays the track automation lanes/envelopes above them as the primary editing layer. Use Hex's existing theme/shared controls and actual automation model; the screenshot is a workflow/layering reference, not a request to copy Live's theme. Inspect current automation display and any existing A binding before changes; preserve authored automation, playback and Undo history when switching view modes. Provide a discoverable mode indicator/control, accurate parameter/lane identity, visible curves/points and clear interaction layering. A must respect text-entry/rename/dialog/control focus and must not insert a character or trigger during ordinary text editing. Toggling back restores clip editing without destroying automation or selection. Bound scope to Arrangement mode and existing supported automation capabilities; report unavailable targets rather than implying new DSP/parameter coverage. Verify real rendered A dispatch, faded-clip/foreground automation geometry and hit routing, toggle round trip, text focus guards and existing automation editing/history/playback contracts. Coordinate one writer for editor/mod.rs, render.rs and track/automation areas before implementation. Source owner to be assigned by coordinator; dedicated merger owns final exact-candidate required local CI and merges, root owns all native/app delivery. No hosted CI, Mac self-dispatch, installed-app operations, migration or duplicate automation engine. Screenshot remains in originating chat; preserve it as reference and attach through supported image tooling when available. Duplicate search of live Hex automation tickets found platform/parameter work #2674 and old #28 but no matching Arrangement A-view toggle.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
